I believe he has....the Grail.	我相信他……手裡有聖杯。
Sir Gawaine shall never speak again.	高文爵士再也無法開口說話了。
Consider how you might best do that.	仔細想想，該如何做才是上策。
Aye, Gawaine must be helped. If he does not reach Camelot soon, he will die of his injuries.	正是，高文亟需救助。他若不能盡快抵達肯萊特，傷勢終將奪去他的性命。
He is beyond help.	他已無藥可救。
First, you must dismount.	首先，你必須下馬。
Uh... surely you have mistaken me... for someone else.	呃……你想必是……認錯人了。
Do not add necrophilia to your list of sins.	莫在你的罪過之上，再添褻瀆亡者之舉。
Have you gone completely mad!?!	你莫非已經瘋了不成！？！
He is already dead.  Your shame is great enough without adding evil thoughts to it.	他已然離世。你的恥辱已經夠深重了，不必再添邪念。
That is hardly what he needs.	這絕非他此刻所需要的。
Though it is a common practice to kiss farewell to the dead, it is hardly right for you to do so when you have caused his death.	雖說親吻亡者道別是常見的習俗，但你正是致他於死的人，此舉實在不妥。
That would cause him even more pain than he is already suffering.	那只會讓他承受比此刻更深的痛楚。
Your sorrow is meaningless.  It will not bring him back from the dead.	你的哀傷毫無意義，不能讓他死而復生。
Aye, he is indeed in need of help.  He will not live hanging from those shackles much longer.	正是，他確實亟需援手。再這樣吊在鎖鏈上，他撐不了多久了。
You have freed him, but he will not live long if left here.	你已將他釋放，但若留他在此，他活不了多久。
Nothing you can do now can wash the sin of Gawaine's death from your soul.	如今你再做什麼，都無法洗淨高文之死加諸你靈魂上的罪。
It may ease your conscience, but will change nothing.	此舉或能寬慰你的良心，卻改變不了任何事。
Let us hope your god heeds your silent prayers.	但願你的神明能聽見你無聲的禱告。
He will go nowhere until free of the shackles.	在鎖鏈解開之前，他哪裡也去不了。
It makes no sense to bear the burden yourself when you have a powerful horse nearby.	身邊既有一匹壯健的坐騎，何必自己扛起這重擔？
Though bearing Gawaine's body is a burden you well deserve, your mission must not be abandoned.  This tree will mark the place where his bones lie.	縱然背負高文的遺體是你理應承受的重擔，你的使命卻不容棄置。這棵樹，將標記他長眠之處。
What does it matter? Gawaine is dead.	這又有什麼要緊？高文已經死了。
Though Gawaine is free of the shackles, his ordeal is far from over. His life depends on your actions, King Arthur.	雖然高文已脫離鎖鏈，他的苦難卻遠未結束。他的性命，繫於你接下來的作為，亞瑟王。
Aye, it would be best to get him free of the shackles as quickly as possible. Seek the most direct method.	正是，當務之急是盡快解開他身上的鎖鏈。尋一個最直截了當的辦法吧。
Better to leave Gawaine's body beneath a tree than slung like baggage on a mule.	與其讓高文的遺體像行囊般掛在騾背上，不如將他安葬於樹下。
King....Arthur....I knew....you would come.	王……亞瑟……我就知道……你會來。
You have shattered the shackles.	你已擊碎了鎖鏈。
May...god be with you, Arthur. Tarry not with me. Go at once....to the Tor. Find...the Grail, I beg you.	願……神與你同在，亞瑟。莫在我身邊耽擱。速速……前往那座山丘。尋得……聖杯，我懇求你。
He is right. Your horse will carry him safely back to Camelot. Even if you must go on foot, you must continue your search without delay, but be assured that this noble sacrifice brings blessings upon you.	他說得對。你的坐騎會平安地將他送回肯萊特。即便你必須徒步前行，也不可耽延你的追尋；但請放心，這番高尚的犧牲，將為你帶來庇佑。
Beware, Arthur! I like not the look of this old hag who stands upon the pedestal.	當心，亞瑟！我不喜歡這座台座上老婦人的模樣。
These are runes of a very ancient type, probably a warning or incantation.	這些是極為古老的符文，恐怕是某種警示或咒語。
An inscription in runes has appeared upon the pedestal where the witch stood.	女巫先前所立的台座上，浮現出一段符文銘刻。
The forest witch stands upon a pedestal of some kind. I cannot say what purpose it may have had, though it does seem to be covered in badly weathered carvings.	森林女巫立在一座台座上。我說不出它原本有何用途，不過台座上似乎滿是風化嚴重的雕刻。
This small stone was once a man, but will never be so again.	這塊小石頭曾是一個人，如今卻再也不會是了。
These large standing stones are megaliths. It means simply 'big stone'.	這些巨大的立石就是巨石。這個詞的意思很簡單，就是『大石頭』。
Ye shall never move again, unless ye offer me what I desire.	汝將永不得動彈，除非獻上我所渴求之物。
Do not be daunted. This reads to me more like an instruction than an incantation. Let your own wits serve you.	莫要氣餒。依我看，這與其說是咒語，更像是一則指引。憑你自己的機智去解讀吧。
The runes might be important. If you ask, I could translate them.	這些符文或許十分重要。你若開口詢問，我可以為你翻譯。
You had best think of something to satisfy the old hag.	你最好想個辦法，滿足這老婦人的要求。
There is no danger within this stone circle now that the witch is gone. Alas, that her previous victims could not be freed.	如今女巫已去，這圈立石之內再無危險。只可惜，她先前的犧牲者已無法獲釋。
There is terrible power in this old hag. She is a forest witch drawing upon the powers within this stone circle.	這老婦人身上蘊藏著可怖的力量。她是森林女巫，汲取著這圈立石之中的力量。
The foliage has crept back from these stones, but it is difficult to see what lies beyond.	枝葉已從這些石頭邊悄悄退去，但仍難以看清外頭有些什麼。
Though human hands once placed these stones, your two hands will not move them.	雖然這些石頭當初是人手所立，但單憑你雙手，是搬不動它們的。
You are not tall enough to do that.	你的身高不夠，做不到這件事。
The sky is open overhead. Not a single tree grows close enough to overhang this stone circle.	頭頂天空一片開闊，沒有一棵樹長得夠近，能遮蔽這圈立石。
Evidently, she has decided to follow you again.	看來，她又決定跟隨你了。
Happily, you have set her free. The witch will not plague this forest again.	值得慶幸的是，你已將她釋放。這女巫再也不會為禍這片森林了。
Those three small stones were once men, but will never be so again.	那三塊小石頭曾是三個人，如今卻再也不會是了。
I fear the lovely lady's search for her beloved knight will end in misery and she will weep o'er his bones.	我恐怕這位佳人尋找心上騎士的旅程，終將以悲劇收場，她只能在他的枯骨前灑淚。
Do you call this ugly and withered old crone a girl? Truly, you have been in this forest too long.	你竟稱這乾癟醜陋的老太婆為姑娘？看來你在這片森林待得太久了。
This circle of standing stones must be at the very edge of the Forest Perilous. But it has no henge, for a henge is a circular embankment.	這圈立石想必正位於派瑞樂斯森林的邊緣。不過它算不上是『環壘』，因為環壘指的是環形的土堤。
There is no monolith, but there are many megaliths.	這裡沒有單一的巨石柱，卻有許多巨石。
The large standing stones are megaliths. It means simply 'big stone'.	這些巨大的立石就是巨石。這個詞的意思很簡單，就是『大石頭』。
They are not pillars, they are standing stones. Unlike a cromlech or dolmen, these are arranged in a circle.	它們不是石柱，而是立石。不同於克倫勒克石冢或支石墓，這些石頭是排成一個圓圈的。
These standing stones have but one entrance which is a trilithon: two upright stones with a capstone or lintel-stone over the top of them.	這些立石只有一處入口，那是一座『三石塔』：兩根直立的石柱，上方架著一塊冠石或楣石。
It means 'three stones' and is a structure of two upright stones capped by a lintel-stone.	這個詞意為『三塊石頭』，指的是兩根直立石柱、上方覆蓋一塊楣石的結構。
Dolmen comes from two Bretogne words: 'tol' meaning 'table' and 'men' meaning 'stone'. It refers to a tomb made of upright stones covered by a slab for a roof, then covered over with soil to make a mound.	『支石墓（dolmen）』一詞源自兩個布列塔尼語詞：'tol' 意為『桌子』，'men' 意為『石頭』。指的是以直立石塊搭建、上覆石板為頂的墳墓，再覆土堆成塚。
Cromlech comes from the Welsh words: 'crom' meaning 'bent' and 'llech' meaning 'flat'. It refers to a tomb made of upright stones covered by a slab for a roof, then covered over with soil to make a mound.	『克倫勒克（cromlech）』一詞源自威爾斯語：'crom' 意為『彎曲』，'llech' 意為『平坦』。指的是以直立石塊搭建、上覆石板為頂的墳墓，再覆土堆成塚。
These are not natural rocks, as should be obvious. They are standing stones arranged in a circle.	顯而易見，這些並非天然岩石，而是排成圓圈的立石。
I regret I know nothing that would help you.	很遺憾，我沒有任何能幫上你的知識。
I cannot. You must rely upon your own wits.	我做不到。你必須仰賴自己的機智。
Cease prattling and give me what I desire.	休再喋喋不休，把我所渴求之物獻上。
Betimes I worry about you, Arthur. You set the Lady Elayne free, remember?	亞瑟，我有時真為你擔心。還記得嗎，你曾釋放過艾蓮公主。
Alas, you cannot.	可惜，你辦不到。
The Lady Elayne seemed much too overjoyed to listen, did she not? Nor would you have taken much pleasure in telling her the sad fate of her beloved knight.	艾蓮公主當時似乎欣喜得聽不進任何話，不是嗎？何況，把她心上騎士的悲慘下場告訴她，你自己也未必忍心。
I know not to whom ye would speak, but ye had best deal with me if ye wish to pass this circle.	我不知汝欲與誰交談，但汝若想通過此圈，最好先應付我。
You will see nothing special from there. You would only obscure the runes carved upon the top of the pedestal.	從那裡你什麼特別的也看不見，只會擋住台座頂端所刻的符文。
Ye must deal with me first!	汝須先應付我！
The runes on the pedestal say this...	台座上的符文寫著……
"Five poets bold Did come astray. Five standing stones Now bar the way. Of limbs bereft, Yet voice I left. To pass through the middle You must ask for......."	「五位大膽詩人，誤入歧途流連。五尊立石而今，擋住去路向前。四肢盡失無存，唯留一縷聲喚。欲從中央穿行，你須開口求……」
Alas, it fades out here. The last flurry of magick which caused it to appear must not have been enough to bring out the full inscription.	可惜，銘文到此便消散了。看來喚出它的那陣法力餘波，並不足以顯現完整的銘刻。
I see no writing here.	我在此處看不見任何文字。
There is nothing left of her, fortunately.	所幸，她已經什麼都不剩了。
And how do ye propose to do that, arrogant one?	汝這狂妄之人，打算如何做到？
That is not what you came here to do. Remember your mission.	你來此並非為了這件事。莫忘你的使命。
I care naught for what ye desire. Give me what I desire.	汝所欲為何，我毫不在乎。把我所渴求之物獻上。
That is beyond your strength.	那超出了你的力量所及。
Too late to think of that.	此刻再想這個，已經太遲了。
I care nothing for pretty words. If ye wish to pass, ye must give me what I desire.	花言巧語於我毫無用處。汝若想通過，就得獻上我所渴求之物。
Betimes I worry about you, Arthur. You set her free, remember?	亞瑟，我有時真為你擔心。還記得嗎，你曾釋放過她。
Ye shall not pass through this circle unless ye give me what I desire.	除非獻上我所渴求之物，汝休想穿過此圈。
And what may this be that I desire, ye wonder? Hah! If ye be so cunning a knight, ye shall know.	汝在想，我所渴求的究竟是何物？哈！汝若真是機智的騎士，自會知曉。
King of paupers! Ye offer nothing.	窮鬼之王！汝獻上的什麼也不是。
If ye would buy a safe passage, ye must offer nothing less than an entire purse.	汝若想以財買得安然通行，非得獻上整個錢囊不可。
For this, I shall let ye pass.	為此，我便放汝通過。
Ye think ye be a grand prize, but ye do not be what I most desire.	汝自以為是件了不起的獻禮，但汝並非我最渴求之物。
Ye be a fool to part with this gift of love, but for it I shall let ye pass.	捨得這份愛的信物，汝真是個傻子，但為此我便放汝通過。
For this magical stone, I shall let ye pass.	為這塊有魔力的石頭，我便放汝通過。
Ye part with the very heart of the Lady of the Lake, but for this gift I shall let ye pass.	汝竟捨得湖中女神的心，但為這份獻禮，我便放汝通過。
Ye please me not with this offer.	這獻禮，不能令我滿意。
Seek ye not to bargain with me. I take, I do not give.	休想與我討價還價。我只取，不予。
If ye be so cunning a knight, ye shall know.	汝若真是機智的騎士，自會知曉。
I care nothing for the petty doings of men. Give me what I desire or ye shall suffer.	凡人瑣事，我毫不在乎。獻上我所渴求之物，否則汝將自食苦果。
Look all ye want, mortal man. These three by me, see ye them? Once they too were men.	看個夠吧，凡人。我身旁這三個，汝可看見？他們也曾是人。
They dared enter my circle, but did not give me what I desired. Will ye end like them?	他們膽敢闖入我的石圈，卻未獻上我所渴求之物。汝也要落得同樣下場嗎？
You cannot get back what you have not given.	你不曾獻出之物，如何取回？
Seek to take back what ye have given and ye shall be stone before ye can blink.	汝若想討回已獻出之物，眨眼間便會化為石頭。
But she does not have it.	但她並沒有這東西。
What ye have given, ye have lost.	汝已獻出之物，便已失去。
It is ye who smell of warm blood and mortal flesh. Ye reek of life. I shall like ye better when ye smell of cold stone.	汝身上散發著溫熱鮮血與凡人血肉的氣味，滿身生氣逼人。待汝渾身化作冰冷石頭的氣味，我才會更喜歡汝。
I think it is you who needs the help.	我看，需要幫助的人是你才對。
It is a good thought, Arthur, but your mission is far more important.	這念頭是好的，亞瑟，但你的使命遠比這重要得多。
Try it if ye dare, arrogant one.	有膽便試試看，狂妄之人。
What a disgusting notion.	多麼令人作嘔的念頭。
Put up thy sword! Put it away this instant or ye shall become stone!	收起汝的劍！立刻收起，否則汝將化為石頭！
Halt! Ye shall not pass me unhindered, king though ye be.	止步！縱然汝貴為國王，也休想毫無阻攔地從我身旁通過。
Aye, rage if you will, but until ye give me what I desire, ye shall not move another step.	盡管動怒吧，但汝若不獻上我所渴求之物，便再也休想向前踏出一步。
And if ye give me not what I desire, a stone ye shall be.	汝若不獻上我所渴求之物，便將化為石頭。
Aye! Aye! That is what I most desire! Bring it here at once!	是了！是了！那正是我最渴求之物！速速取來獻上！
Bless you, valiant knight! I am the Lady Elayne, transformed into the forest witch by a hideous spell cast upon me by the Black Knight.	感謝你，英勇的騎士！我是艾蓮公主，被黑武士施下的邪惡咒語，變成了這森林女巫。
Only this sleeve, which I gave to my true love, could set me free.	唯有這件我贈予真愛之人的衣袖，才能使我獲得解脫。
And if my sleeve is here, my beloved knight cannot be far away. I must find him at once! Fare thee well!	既然我的衣袖在此，我心愛的騎士必定就在不遠處。我得立刻去尋他！珍重了！
Now be gone!	如今，去吧！
No man can best me with cold steel. Pay the price for thy arrogance.	無人能憑冷冽鋼刃勝過我。為汝的狂妄，付出代價吧。
A tongue so foul should never utter another vowel!	如此污穢的舌頭，再不配吐出一個字音！
Ye have not given me what I desire. Stone ye shall be for all eternity!	汝未獻上我所渴求之物。汝將永世化為石頭！
Defeated by an ugly crone, From mortal man to standing stone, With sun and rain upon you blown, 	被一個醜陋的老太婆擊敗，從血肉之軀化為佇立的石頭，任由日曬雨淋加諸其身，
Through carven locks the wind shall moan, Here you will be through years unknown, And slowly crumble when time has flown.	風聲將在你雕鑿的髮絲間低吟，你將在此屹立千古歲月，直到光陰流逝，你才緩緩崩塌碎裂。
Your sudden disappearance was too much for even your well-trained horse. He has run all the way back to Camelot.	你的突然消失，饒是你那匹訓練有素的坐騎，也承受不住，牠已一路奔回肯萊特了。
The eerie glow must mean that you have solved this stone's riddle.	這詭異的光芒，想必意味著你已解開這塊石頭的謎題。
I cannot help you here.	此處我幫不上你。
What riddle? Your request is a riddle to me.	什麼謎題？你這要求對我來說才是個謎。
Only so much help can I give. This is your test and yours alone.	我能給的幫助有限。這是屬於你自己的考驗，唯你一人能過。
There is some sort of sorcerous barrier barring you from the Tor.	有某種巫術屏障，擋住了你通往那座山丘的路。
There are no markings or carvings upon them. They are quite plain.	它們上頭並無任何標記或雕刻，樸實無華。
The only riddle to read here is that there is no riddle here to read.	此處唯一的謎題，就是這裡根本沒有謎題可讀。
You are once more at the base of Glastonbury Tor.	你再次來到格列斯登伯利山腳下。
You have reached the base of Glastonbury Tor on the edge of the Forest Perilous.	你已抵達派瑞樂斯森林邊緣、格列斯登伯利山的山腳下。
And I see your mule grazes as it waits for you. She must have found her way safely through the forest on her own.	我看見你的騾子正一邊吃草一邊等你。牠想必是自己安然穿過了這片森林。
